[{:registry/operating-states [:intake :propose :approve :execute :audit], :actor/wave 3, :registry/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-ledger], :actor/scope-excluded-ops [:finalize-weaving-decision :finalize-weaving-operation :finalize-knitting-operation :authorize-loom-run :authorize-knitting-run :proceed-with-weaving-run :proceed-with-knitting-run :finalize-mill-safety-clearance :declare-machine-safe-for-operation :declare-fabric-batch-safe-for-shipment :clear-batch-for-shipment :override-mill-safety-officer-judgment :override-safety-officer-judgment], :actor/robotics? true, :adr/related ["adr-2607121000-cloud-itonami-global-isic-isco-reverse-toposort-plan" "adr-2799008122-cloud-itonami-isco-8122-metal-finishing-plating-coating-machine-operators-coverage"], :adr/status :accepted, :actor/scope-excluded-terms ["proceed with the weaving run" "proceed with the knitting run" "authorize the loom run" "authorize the knitting run" "finalize the weaving decision" "finalize the weaving operation" "finalize the knitting operation" "declare the machine safe for operation" "declare the loom safe for operation" "declare the knitting machine safe for operation" "declare the fabric batch safe for shipment" "declare the batch safe for shipment" "clear the batch for shipment" "clear the fabric batch for shipment" "finalize the mill safety clearance" "declare the mill safety cleared" "override the mill safety officer's judgment" "override the safety officer's judgment" "override mill safety officer judgment"], :adr/id 2799008152, :phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:log-work-record :flag-safety-concern :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order}, :auto #{:log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation}}}", :actor/domain :manufacturing/weaving-knitting-mill-scheduling-logistics-coordination, :actor/proposal-ops [:log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order], :actor/hard-checks [:no-weaver :no-mill :no-actuation :unknown-op :scope-excluded-action], :registry/maturity :implemented, :actor/isco-08 "8152", :actor/always-escalate-ops [:flag-safety-concern], :adr/doc_type "adr", :operation/nodes [:intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold], :operation/entry-point :intake, :adr/body "# ADR 2799008152: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 8152 Weaving and Knitting Machine Operators mill scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 8152\n-- Weaving and Knitting Machine Operators** only. This is Wave3\n(production/trades); Wave0/1/2 are 100% complete, the entire 75xx\ncraft-trades range is complete, and this actor extends the 81xx\nstationary-plant/machine-operator range into the 815x textile/fur/\nleather products machine operators sub-group (`kotoba.occupation.wave/\nwave-of \"8152\"` resolves to wave 3).\n\n`gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8152` returned a clean\n404 before any work began -- this was a genuinely fresh scaffold, not a\nresume of prior partial work. A check for the intended reference\nrepository `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8151` (Fibre Preparing,\nSpinning and Winding Machine Operators) also returned 404 (not yet\nlanded by its sibling agent in this batch), so this actor instead\nmirrors `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8122` (Metal Finishing,\nPlating and Coating Machine Operators), independently re-cloned and\nread in full this session.\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"8152\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-\noccupation \\\"8152\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Weaving and Knitting Machine\nOperators\" -- confirming the premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR\nthe entry's `:maturity` was `:spec` with `:required-technologies\n[:robotics :identity :audit-ledger]` and no `:repo`/`:business-id`.\nThis ADR and its companion registry edit promote the `8152` entry to\n`:implemented`.\n\n**Textile-machinery entanglement hazard dimension.** Weaving and\nKnitting Machine Operators run high-speed loom and knitting equipment\n-- a real entanglement hazard from moving shuttles, needles and drive\nmechanisms, alongside sustained noise exposure. This actor does NOT\nmodel direct weaving/knitting-equipment operation authority or\nmill-safety-clearance authority. It is deliberately restricted to MILL\nSCHEDULING and LOGISTICS COORDINATION around the occupation\n(production-run/inventory/progress-record logging, crew/shift\nscheduling, safety-concern escalation, and yarn/thread-stock\nprocurement coordination) -- never the machine-operation-execution\ndecision or the mill-safety-clearance decision itself, and never an\noverride of a mill safety officer's judgment. The closed proposal-op\nallowlist structurally excludes any op that could directly finalize\nsuch a decision, and the governor independently, permanently\nhard-blocks any proposal whose rationale text names such a\nfinalization action, regardless of the declared `:op` or confidence --\nthis is not an escalation path a human can approve through, it is an\noutright, structural refusal at every maturity level.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8122`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8122)\n(Metal Finishing, Plating and Coating Machine Operators -- a closely\nrelated hazardous-machinery scheduling/logistics coordination\npattern). Its `platingcoord.{store,advisor,governor,actor}` module\nsplit, `langgraph.graph` StateGraph shape, closed op-allowlist and\nscope-exclusion self-trip-guard design translate almost 1:1 onto this\noccupation's own entanglement-hazard-adjacent coordination scope, so\nthis ADR's `millcoord.*` modules follow the same shape with domain\nterms substituted (plater -> weaver, plating facility/plant -> mill,\nplant safety officer -> mill safety officer, plating-operation-\nexecution -> machine-operation-execution, chemical-safety-clearance ->\nmill-safety-clearance).\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8152` as an OSS\ndocumentation/logistics-coordination actor for weaving and knitting\nmachine operators, following the SAME governed-actor architecture as\nevery prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this fleet: **Mill\nScheduling Coordination Advisor ⊣ MillCoordGovernor** on a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph (`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`,\ngit-sha-pinned identically to the reference's `deps.edn` -- a\ndifferent library coordinate from the `langgraph-clj` used by the\nunrelated `20-actors/*` actor family), with an independent Governor,\nhuman-in-the-loop approval via `interrupt-before`, and an append-only\naudit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **mill scheduling/logistics coordination\nONLY, never weaving/knitting-equipment operation authority** -- it\nmust NEVER be designed to exercise, simulate exercising, or propose\nexercising a machine-operation-execution decision or a\nmill-safety-clearance decision.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- production-run/inventory/progress data\n  logging only\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/shift/task scheduling proposal\n  only\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface an entanglement-hazard/noise-\n  exposure/equipment-condition concern, ALWAYS escalates immediately,\n  NEVER auto-commit-eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- yarn/thread-stock procurement proposal\n  only\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase,\nresembles a machine-operation-execution finalization decision or a\nmill-safety-clearance finalization decision -- these are structurally\nabsent from the op-allowlist entirely, not merely gated behind\nescalation.\n\n### Five HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Weaver unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered weaver (crew member) record\n   (`:no-weaver`). Never trusts the proposal's own claim of who the\n   weaver is.\n2. **Mill unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered weaving/knitting mill/line record\n   (`:no-mill`).\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (`:no-actuation`; the governor never dispatches hardware\n   itself and never operates weaving/knitting equipment itself).\n4. **Op not allowed** -- any `:op` outside the closed four-op\n   allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`).\n5. **Scope-excluded action** -- the proposal's `:op` or `:rationale`\n   must never name a machine-operation-execution finalization, a\n   mill-safety-clearance finalization, or a mill-safety-officer-\n   judgment override (`:scope-excluded-action`), REGARDLESS of the\n   declared `:op` or confidence. This is a hard, PERMANENT block --\n   there is no maturity level or confidence at which this actor may\n   auto-commit or human-approve its way past this rule; it is an\n   outright refusal, not an escalation.\n\n### Escalation gates (always human sign-off)\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's always-escalate path). The only channel by\n  which the robot may surface an entanglement-hazard/noise-exposure/\n  equipment-condition observation -- it never resolves the concern\n  itself.\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (2000) -- always needs human sign-off,\n  independent of confidence (boundary verified as exclusive by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`: exactly-at-threshold\n  commits, over-threshold escalates).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, CLAUDE.md)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as bare NOUNS (e.g.\n\"loom\", \"shuttle\", \"needle\") can accidentally match inside the mock\nadvisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate proposal,\nself-blocking the actor's own happy path -- and this vertical's domain\nvocabulary is an especially sharp case of that risk, because routine\nwork-log/task text legitimately names loom/knitting-machine components\nby name (e.g. a task literally described as \"routine loom shuttle and\nknitting needle maintenance task with yarn/thread-stock check\" --\nequipment identification, not a proposal to finalize a weaving/\nknitting run or clear a machine as safe). `millcoord.governor/scope-\nexcluded-phrases` is phrased exclusively as finalization ACTION\nPHRASES (\"proceed with the weaving run\", \"finalize the weaving\noperation\", \"declare the mill safety cleared\", \"override the mill\nsafety officer's judgment\"), never bare nouns, and is checked only\nagainst the proposal's `:rationale` field (the advisor's own generated\ntext), never against raw `:task` input text.\n`millcoord.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-\ntrip-on-scope-exclusion` is a dedicated regression test driving the\ndefault mock-advisor across all four allowed ops with a task field\ncontaining exactly those bare equipment nouns, asserting none of them\never hard-trip the finalization-scope rule. Green on first run.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"8152\" ...}` entry\n  promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id`\n  set to the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8152` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-8152`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary` immediately before the edit,\n  not assumed, to account for concurrent sibling landings in this same\n  6-agent batch).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 34 tests, 73 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's `:test/\n  counts` and independently re-verified against a brand-new fresh\n  clone of the pushed repository (not just the local working copy). No\n  mojibake in the Japanese violation-detail strings (0\n  replacement-byte instances grepped in the fresh clone).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely\n  via the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent\n  with sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`) -- a single-entity EDN vector with an\n  `:adr/body` string blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-weaving-run`/`:approve-mill-\n  safety-clearance` that is merely gated behind an always-escalate\n  path: rejected outright per the task's explicit guidance -- an\n  always-escalate op still means the *capability* to finalize a\n  weaving/knitting operation or a mill-safety clearance exists in the\n  code path and is merely deferred to a human gate. For a decision\n  whose failure mode is entanglement injury or hearing damage, the\n  capability itself must not exist in this actor at all.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"loom\" \"shuttle\"\n  \"needle\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known self-trip bug\n  class described above -- this domain's own vocabulary necessarily\n  discusses loom/knitting-machine components by name to do its\n  logging/scheduling job, so a bare-noun list would self-block the\n  actor's own legitimate proposals whenever a task description\n  mentions loom or knitting-machine parts.\n- Naming the crew-member field `:operator-id` (matching the ISCO title\n  \"...Machine Operators\" literally): rejected -- `docs/operator-\n  guide.md` and this fleet's convention already use \"operator\" to mean\n  the deploying business/entity running the actor, so reusing the same\n  word for the individual crew member would create a confusing\n  collision (mirroring the reference's `:plater-id` vs. \"operator\"\n  precedent); `:weaver-id` keeps the two senses distinct.\n\n## Test verification\n\nFresh clone re-run immediately before writing this ADR:\n\n```text\nRunning tests in #{\"test\"}\n\nTesting millcoord.actor-test\n\nTesting millcoord.governor-test\n\nRan 34 tests containing 73 assertions.\n0 failures, 0 errors.\n```\n", :adr/date "2026-07-18", :test/counts "{:total 34, :assertions 73, :failures 0, :errors 0}", :actor/coordination? true, :actor/name "Weaving and Knitting Mill Scheduling and Logistics Coordination Practice", :db/id -1, :test/coverage [:governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :weaver-verification :mill-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation :machine-operation-mill-safety-clearance-finalization-forbidden :mill-safety-officer-override-forbidden], :registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-8152", :registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8152", :adr/scope [:kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8152], :test/simulator :millcoord.actor-test, :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-8152 — Weaving and Knitting Machine Operators Mill Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/references [2607121000], :actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-8152}]
